A small Shinto shrine inside the Tenryuji Temple complex, as the light fades into the night.

</p>
<p class="jp">
天龍寺の境内にある小さな神社だ。薄明かりが夜に溶けていく頃。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Arashiyama" /><category term="Shrines" /><category term="Dusk" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A small Shinto shrine inside the Tenryuji Temple complex, as the light fades into the night.]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_A7R08254.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_A7R08254.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Temple View・寺からの眺め</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261016/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Temple View・寺からの眺め" /><published>2026-10-16T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-16T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/temple-view</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261016/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
From Arashiyama mountain we can see the city in the distance. At left is Mt. Hiei across the city, below is the Oigawa River. Taken from Daihikaku Senkoji temple.
</p>
<p class="jp">
嵐山から、遠くに街並みが見える。左手には、街並みの向こうに比叡山が見え、眼下には大堰川が流れている。大悲閣千光寺から撮影した。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Arashiyama" /><category term="Katsura River" /><category term="Aerial" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[From Arashiyama mountain we can see the city in the distance. At left is Mt. Hiei across the city, below is the Oigawa River. Taken from Daihikaku Senkoji temple. 嵐山から、遠くに街並みが見える。左手には、街並みの向こうに比叡山が見え、眼下には大堰川が流れている。大悲閣千光寺から撮影した。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100269.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100269.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Arashiyama Dusk・夕暮れの嵐山</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261015/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Arashiyama Dusk・夕暮れの嵐山" /><published>2026-10-15T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-15T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/arashiyama</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261015/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
The end of the day in Arashiyama.
</p>
<p class="jp">
嵐山での一日の終わりだ。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Arashiyama" /><category term="Dusk" /><category term="Boats" /><category term="Katsura River" /><category term="Togetsu Bridge" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The end of the day in Arashiyama. 嵐山での一日の終わりだ。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100259.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100259.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Tokyo Station・東京駅</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261014/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Tokyo Station・東京駅" /><published>2026-10-14T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-14T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/tokyo-station</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261014/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
A recent photo of the Marunouchi entrance to Tokyo Station (1914) in the afternoon sun.
</p>
<p class="jp">
午後の日差しを浴びた、東京駅丸の内口（1914年竣工）の最近撮影された写真。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Tokyo" /><category term="Trains" /><category term="Architecture" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A recent photo of the Marunouchi entrance to Tokyo Station (1914) in the afternoon sun. 午後の日差しを浴びた、東京駅丸の内口（1914年竣工）の最近撮影された写真。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100193.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100193.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Yuka・川床</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261013/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Yuka・川床" /><published>2026-10-13T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-13T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/kawayuka</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261013/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
These are the last warm sunny days in Kyoto. Soon the temporary outdoor dining platforms along the river  (<em>yuka</em> or <em>kawadoko</em>) will be taken down for the winter.
</p>
<p class="jp">
京都では、暖かく晴れた日々も残りわずかとなった。まもなく、川沿いに設けられた仮設の屋外席、川床(ゆか・かわどこ)も、冬を前に撤去される。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Kyoto" /><category term="Night" /><category term="Kamo River" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[These are the last warm sunny days in Kyoto. Soon the temporary outdoor dining platforms along the river (yuka or kawadoko) will be taken down for the winter. 京都では、暖かく晴れた日々も残りわずかとなった。まもなく、川沿いに設けられた仮設の屋外席、川床(ゆか・かわどこ)も、冬を前に撤去される。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100244.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100244.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Togetsukyo・渡月橋</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261012/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Togetsukyo・渡月橋" /><published>2026-10-12T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-12T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/togetsukyo</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261012/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
Arashiyama's Togetsu Bridge illuminated by the early morning light.
</p>
<p class="jp">
早朝の光に照らされた嵐山の渡月橋。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Arashiyama" /><category term="Togetsu Bridge" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Arashiyama's Togetsu Bridge illuminated by the early morning light. 早朝の光に照らされた嵐山の渡月橋。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100212.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_RX100212.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry><entry><title type="html">Kemari・蹴鞠</title><link href="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261011/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Kemari・蹴鞠" /><published>2026-10-11T00:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-11T00:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://hermosawavephotography.com/kemari</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://hermosawavephotography.com/261011/"><![CDATA[<p class="en">
A ceremonial game of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kemari" target="_blank">Kemari</a>, a game from the 7th Century similar to hacky sack, played in Heian era robes at Kyoto's Imperial Palace.
</p>
<p class="jp">
    京都御所で、平安時代の装束を身にまとって行われる、7世紀に起源を持つハッキーサックに似た遊び「<a href="https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/蹴鞠" target="_blank">蹴鞠</a>」の儀式。
</p>]]></content><author><name>Daniel Sofer</name></author><category term="Kyoto" /><category term="Imperial Palace" /><category term="Sports" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A ceremonial game of Kemari, a game from the 7th Century similar to hacky sack, played in Heian era robes at Kyoto's Imperial Palace. 京都御所で、平安時代の装束を身にまとって行われる、7世紀に起源を持つハッキーサックに似た遊び「蹴鞠」の儀式。]]></summary><media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_A7R08035_edit.jpg" /><media:content medium="image" url="https://hermosawavephotography.com/assets/images/2026/2610_A7R08035_edit.jpg" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" /></entry></feed>